              "current": "- **Thin launch liquidity.** When the token market opens, it starts SMALL by design. Ordinary trades can move the\n  price, and a round trip pays base fees on both legs, LP fees, any sell surcharge and slippage. Do not treat the pool as an exit for\n  size.\n- **Canonical-pool trades pay fees.** The restricted manager charges a fixed 3.5% base plus a separate 0.5% native ETH staking rewards allocation on buys and sells. The Hook can add up to 0.5% sell-pressure surcharge, for a maximum protocol charge of 4.5%. On exact-input sells, 4% comes off the top of actual ETH output as the ordinary protocol charge. Exact-input swaps pay from actual output (buy: OMR; sell: ETH), while exact-output swaps add the charge to actual input (buy: ETH; sell: OMR). Partial fills use actual settled amounts. These rates and recipients are fixed, with no Committee or Safe fee-change queue. The planned genesis pool adds a static 0.3% LP fee; LP fees and network gas are additional. Every ETH/OMR pool admitted by this manager pays the base and native ETH staking rewards allocation; independent third-party venues require separate verification.\n  The separate game-withdrawal surcharge applies to balances younger than 48 hours, charging\n  up to an extra 50% that fades to zero across that window; it does not apply to ordinary wallet holding.\n- **Withdrawing will pay a toll and can queue.** Once production extraction opens, every on-chain withdrawal pays a flat 2% toll, and the\n",
