              "current": "    <h1>Where the fees go</h1>\n    <p class=\"sub\">Try a fee allocation. Change each source's split, trace its destinations, then export your proposal.</p>\n  </header>\n  <div class=\"scenario-notice\"><b>This is an illustrative scenario, not current production.</b> The current restricted-manager policy charges a fixed 3.5% base on buys and sells: 1.27% developer, 0.51% RWA, 0.76% community and 0.96% POL, with rounding remainder assigned to POL. A separate 0.5% allocation funds native ETH staking rewards, making the ordinary protocol charge 4%. Native ETH rewards use time-weighted unwithdrawn OMR stake. Each deposit has a 30-day minimum withdrawal lock. Matured principal continues earning until withdrawn, without renewal. Stake, mature withdrawal and reward claim have zero protocol tax; network gas applies. Thirty-day reward periods become claimable after closing and finalization. The Hook adds a sell-pressure surcharge of at most 0.5%, for a maximum protocol charge of 4.5%, without collecting the base or rewards twice. LP fees and network gas are additional. The planned genesis pool uses a separate static 0.3% LP fee; its opening buy charges and caps are disabled. Base rates, allocation shares and recipients are fixed for the deployment; local edits cannot become an executable Committee or Safe fee-change proposal. Inventory-bond proceeds, surge receipts and the arbitrage reserve share fund the War Chest; the base POL fee funds Core. ETH and OMR receipts are separate, and each currency row is an example; exact-input fees use actual output and exact-output fees use actual input. Character creation proceeds go 100% to DEV_WALLET. The payment router divides ETH from respawn, reroll and Store purchases into 50% for the developer, 25% for the Vig, 10% for Treasury and 15% for the community. Game withdrawal charges follow their own schedule. All edits stay in this browser; they cannot change policy, move money or open extraction. Production trading remains inactive. Read the <a href=\"/wiki#canonical-market\">current market mechanics</a> and <a href=\"/wiki#chain\">production rail status</a>.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"scenario-notice\"><b>Approved genesis terms, subject to deployment and launch verification.</b> One five-day ETH/OMR auction admits paid or free-credit character NFT holders without individual allocation caps. The 100M allocation is 40M offered, 20M for initial liquidity and 40M held at the Safe until bond activation; unsold sale tokens are tracked separately. The successful-raise minimum is 10 ETH. Half of accepted ETH funds liquidity at the funded asset ratio, independently of the last auction price; all remaining accepted ETH credits the Safe’s Family Yield treasury. Successful-auction filled tokens are claimable at closure after bid exit, without waiting for LP migration; completed purchases are final and unused ETH is returned. Read <a href=\"/wiki#genesis\">the full terms and native-clock timing</a>.</div>\n\n",
