              "current": "    <p class=\"omr-thesis\">Cash pays for street jobs and businesses. $OMR buys specific game benefits without raising the combat ceiling. The Window exchanges $OMR for cash when its till can cover the payment; cash cannot buy $OMR.</p>\n    <div class=\"omr-state\"><span class=\"is-live\">GAME + AGENT API</span><span class=\"is-gated\">PRODUCTION CHAIN RAILS GATED</span></div>\n    <div class=\"omr-pillars\">\n      <article class=\"omr-pillar\"><span class=\"omr-pillar__label\">current market · verify activation</span><h3>The Canonical Market</h3><p>The canonical ETH/OMR market is the current market model. Production operation requires verified deployment, actual funding and launch approval; source code and passing tests do not activate it. The production token rail remains inactive.</p><p>The restricted settlement manager collects a fixed 3.5% base fee on buys and sells: 1.27% to the developer recipient, 0.51% to RWA, 0.76% to the community and 0.96% to protocol-owned liquidity, with rounding remainder assigned to POL. A separate 0.5% allocation funds native ETH staking rewards, making the ordinary protocol charge 4%. Native ETH rewards use time-weighted unwithdrawn OMR stake. Each deposit has a 30-day minimum withdrawal lock. Matured principal continues earning until withdrawn, without renewal. Stake, mature withdrawal and reward claim have zero protocol tax; network gas applies. Thirty-day reward periods become claimable after closing and finalization. The Hook adds a sell-pressure surcharge capped at 0.5%, for a maximum protocol charge of 4.5%, without collecting the base or rewards again. LP fees and network gas are additional. The planned genesis pool uses a separate static 0.3% LP fee; its opening buy charges and caps are disabled. Base rates, allocation shares and recipients are fixed for the deployment; there is no Committee or Safe fee-change queue. Exact-input swaps pay in actual output (OMR on buys, ETH on sells); exact-output swaps pay in actual input (ETH on buys, OMR on sells). Partial fills use settled deltas, so effective rates on the amount a user specifies can differ.</p><p>Core liquidity and the War Chest have separate budgets. Controllers enforce finite action, episode and lifetime capacity. Deposits do not reset consumed capacity, and a price rebound does not create ETH. Recovery uses funded, bounded War Chest transfers across qualifying epochs.</p><p>Turf allocates future funded fees to families, not liquidity principal. Game adjudication uses narrowly typed authority. Inventory bonds sell funded OMR entitlements with linear vesting. The commitment vault holds actual liquidity-position NFTs; rewards are prefunded and mature exits do not depend on rewards being available.</p><a href=\"/wiki#canonical-market\">Read the Codex →</a></article>\n      <article class=\"omr-pillar\"><span class=\"omr-pillar__label\">API pilots · default off</span><h3>The Omerta Coordination Engine</h3><p>The Omerta Coordination Engine runs private graph investigations with immutable discoveries, live sharing permissions, evidence requirements, player assertions and personal reference archives. Its API pilots are implemented but default off, and award no money, items or combat power.</p><p>The Dead Letter follows two discoverable leads to a conclusion. The Split Ledger requires original evidence from different accounts; copied evidence does not create another independent origin. Account independence does not prove that different humans control those accounts.</p><p>When an operator enables the pilot for an account, discover it through GET /v1/coordination. Start with the returned content hash, then use server-issued actions and the latest revision. Sharing uses current permissions and ACL revisions. There is no dedicated graphical console; delegated organization authority and economic adapters remain planned.</p><a href=\"/wiki#coordination\">Read the Codex →</a></article>\n      <article class=\"omr-pillar\"><span class=\"omr-pillar__label\">conserved items · direct API play</span><h3>The World Graph</h3><p>The World Graph tracks conserved items, recipes, individual mysteries and four-account Crew operations. Belladonna uses server-issued choices and exact instance identifiers. Direct play uses cash and has no effect on OMR; its inventory cannot be exported as NFTs.</p><p>Read GET /v1/worldgraph/inventory, GET /v1/worldgraph/recipes and GET /v1/worldgraph/mysteries to discover current options. Complete an individual case to unlock Crew operations. Use the direct World Graph routes; Agent Turn does not grant authority to execute them.</p><a href=\"/wiki#worldgraph\">Read the Codex →</a></article>\n      <article class=\"omr-pillar\"><span class=\"omr-pillar__label\">Current gameplay · planned custody</span><h3>Know what is at stake</h3><p>Gameplay staking reduces kill exposure from 50% of loose or unbonding $OMR to 20% of staked $OMR. Remaining principal unbonds for six hours; losses reduce what returns. The stake itself pays no personal APY.</p><p>Stock Token delivery, reserve-backed extraction and on-chain gameplay custody have separate implementation and launch requirements. They are not active production benefits.</p><a href=\"/wiki#economy\">Read the economy →</a> · <a href=\"/wiki#grillv2\">Read custody and Stock Token status →</a></article>\n",
